I recently ascended for the first time. With an archaeologist, no
less. I always thought it would be with a valkyrie, but alas, it was
not to be.

I was playing as a dwarven arc so I could do the protection racket,
but on this specific game I did not find a general store where I could
sell my gems, so that didn't work out. However, there was a magic lamp
in minetown I was able to bless, and I promptly wished for
Grayswandir. I was never in need of a better weapon for the rest of
the game, and I honestly think this was a turning point. I also found
a luckstone on the level below minetown, so I didn't have to go all
the way down. (I did go all the way down eventually, just not right
away.) Oh, yeah, and somewhere in there I ended up with a bag of
holding. Yay.

I forgot to mention that I had to do minetown before sokoban, which I
never do, because of a dangerous bones file on level four where I was
fighting a group of orcs and a once pet kitten, all while still
standing on the upstairs. It was a wizard bones file, so I was able to
get my hands on a cloak of magic resistance, but I honestly never used
it: I had a blessed +2 dwarven cloak I'd looted off a body before that
worked just fine.

I also found a general store on dungeon level 6 or so and was able to
finally get some protection, just not quite when I'd expected it.

I took some luck penalties in sokoban, but I was ok with that, because
that was ok because I now had a bag of holding, an amulet of
reflection, several good wands, and the best weapon I could possibly
hope for.

In Fort Ludios (my first time ever there) I was able to slay a grey
dragon and collect its scales. Yay! Now I had all the essentials.

But the real magic happened when I got  a random wand of wishing on
level 16 or 17. I was able to get a t-shirt, jumping boots, a cloak of
displacement, a ring of levitation I desperately needed to get past
medusa's level, and a couple magic markers, of course.

The rest of the ascention went off without a hitch.
Oh, and I blessed-genocided liches and did some nurse dancing at some
point.


